  "lineage": "American and British background-jazz practice codified for hotel dining rooms, supper clubs and later for radio and streaming programming from the mid-1950s onward, growing out of cocktail piano and the Nat King Cole and George Shearing trio formats — 70-120 BPM medium swing and bossa feels, brushed drums, walking bass at low dynamics, sparse block-chord piano or vibraphone comping, warm subtone tenor obbligato and either wordless or crooned standards delivered without hard attack.",
